<title>EGYPT: Lucent to add 260,000 lines in Egypt.</title>
<headline>Lucent to add 260,000 lines in Egypt.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. telecommunication firm Lucent Technologies signed a memorandum of understanding with the Egyptian government to set up 260,000 telephones lines in the capital.</p>
<p>The project is to be executed in the next two years and it comes as part of a five-year plan to add five million lines whole of the country, U.S. Commerce Secretary Micky Cantor, who witnessed the signing, told reporters.</p>
</text>
